context_pm1:
Now is the time for a true reflection on the role of the Organization in the twenty-first century, since it is on the United Nations that humankind places much faith and hope for a better life for all. The pall of despair that descended on the world following the Second World War was eased by our forebears’ adoption of lofty ideals when they came together in San Francisco and resolved
“to save succeeding generations from the scourge of war;
“to reaffirm faith in fundamental human rights, in the dignity and worth of the human person, in the equal rights of men and women and of nations large and small, and;
“to promote social progress and better standards of life in larger freedom”. Sadly, today we speak of a world that is slowly regressing to resembling the one that existed seven decades ago.

